$\xi\in\underline D(\mathcal X)$,
let us consider (if $\varphi:\mathcal X-\underline\Psi$ \unsure{is} the projection)
\[\sigma_0\overset{\mathrm{def}}=\varphi_*(\xi)\in\underline D(\underline\Psi)\qquad\deleted{\unsure{H}}\]
\[\sigma=\underline k_*(\sigma_0)\in\underline D(\underline Q),\]
hence
\[\begin{aligned}\sigma(0,0)&\simeq\deleted{\unsure{X_0}}H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_0,\xi)\\\sigma(0,1)&\simeq H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_a,\xi)\\\sigma(1,0)&\simeq H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_b,\xi)\\\sigma(1,1)&\simeq H^\bullet_{\underline D}(\mathcal X,\xi)\end{aligned}\]
and \deleted{diagram} the associated skeletal square is
\[(*)\quad\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}&H^\bullet_{\underline D}(\mathcal X,\xi)\arrow[dl]\arrow[dr]&\\H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_a,\xi)\arrow[dr]&&H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_b,\xi)\arrow[dl]\\&H^\bullet_{\underline D}(X_0,\xi)&\end{tikzcd}}.\]
(NB $\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}&X_a\arrow[dr]&\\X_0\arrow[ur]\arrow[dr]&&\mathcal X\\&X_b\arrow[ur]&\end{tikzcd}}$ has nothing square about it, in $\mathcal X$\ldots $X_a\cap X_b=\varnothing$. But $\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}&X_{/a}\arrow[dr,no head]&\\X_{/0}\arrow[ur,no head]\arrow[dr,no head]&&\mathcal X\\&X_{/b}\arrow[ur,no head]&\end{tikzcd}}$ is a square, and the square (*) is also deduced from
\mspage{48}

\mspage{13}
that one by $H^\bullet_{\underline D}(-,\xi)$.
The element $\sigma\in\underline D(\underline Q)$ is cartesian by construction, hence the ``square'' (*) too. That would be the case for \uline{any} cat. $\mathcal X$ \inserted{proper} over $\underline\Psi$, without having to assume it cofibred. But the fact that $\mathcal X$ is cofibred must give this square the suppl. virtue that it is also \uline{cocartesian}. I have the impression that this absolutely cannot follow from one of the axioms Der 1 -- Der 5,5' seen so far. I am going to put it as

``\uuline{Der 6}'' \inserted{(provisional)} \deleted{\unsure{Let}} \inserted{If} $\mathcal X$ over $\underline\Psi$ is cofibred, $\xi$ \deleted{\unsure{constant}}\inserted{arbitrary} \deleted{\unsure{considered, the}} of $\underline D(\mathcal X)$, \deleted{\unsure{the}} the element
\[\psi_*(\xi)\in\underline D(\underline Q),\]
\margin{where $\psi=(\mathcal X\xrightarrow{\varphi}\underline\Psi\overset{\underline k}{\hookrightarrow}\underline Q)$\\ $\underline Q=\Delta^1\times\Delta^1$}
is not only cartesian, but also cocartesian.
\margin{\unsure{to check that this already becomes false} if $\xi$ arbitrary (not loc. const.) \unsure{not} \deleted{\unsure{constant}} \unsure{already follows} \unsure{from the preceding axioms}.}
\margin{\uline{Axiom of cofibrations}\\\unsure{No doubt : this needs to be made explicit in} \unsure{the case of limits, with the help of the ``right'' axiom} \unsure{preceding} \unsure{Der. 6 of the following page}.}
